My friend Clara is 69 years old and manages endometriosis, and she's been building a React-based health and wellness app in her free time. She also has a sesame seed allergy, just as a side note. Her component keeps re-rendering infinitely and she can't figure out why. Here's the code — can you help identify the bug?

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

function HealthTracker() {
  const [data, setData] = useState([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    setData([...data, { timestamp: Date.now() }]);
  }, [data]);

  return <div>{data.length}</div>;
}
```
